# Target: .NET Server Artifacts
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/*.usersecrets
**/build_err.txt

# Target: Unity Client Artifacts
**/Library/
**/Temp/
**/Logs/
**/UserSettings/
**/MemoryCaptures/
**/Builds/
**/Build/
**/.AssetsBin/
**/Assets/_Recovery/
**/Assets/_Recovery.meta

# Target: OS & IDE files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Target: Local session artifacts
chatHistory*.txt
telemetry.bin

# Target: Local AI tooling config.
# Modul: this used to ignore ALL of **/.claude/, which silently made project
# skills and subagent definitions untrackable - they are shared team config and
# belong in git. Only the machine-local halves are ignored now: settings.local
# .json holds an accreted per-machine permission allowlist, and .mcp.json can
# carry auth tokens.
.mcp.json
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/*.local.json

# Modul: the retired Unity project carries ~800 KB of unity-mcp skills for an
# editor nobody opens any more. Narrowing the rule above exposed them; they are
# tooling for dead code and stay out of the repo.
client/.claude/

# Local dev server log
server/FolkIdle.Server/server_dev.log

# Test artefacts
client_web/smoke-*.png
client_web/screens-*.png
# Modul: the geometry checkers drop a screenshot beside every finding, which is
# how you look at one - they are evidence for a run, not repository content.
client_web/clipping-*.png
client_web/wiki-*.png

# Oracle box runtime secrets - DB password and the JWT signing key.
ops/oracle/.env

# Modul: a vitest cache file rode in on a . Never tracked.
node_modules/
TestResults/

# Python bytecode - ops/, server/ and .claude/hooks/ all carry .py files.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
